    "linked_commit_shas": [
      "de79acaa918c45df358faec1dfbb04b43ef4ab80"
    ],
    "linked_prs": [
      {
        "pr_number": 7,
        "title": "fix header inclusion issues on STM32U545 series",
        "state": "closed",
        "merged": true,
        "github_url": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32u5xx-hal-driver/pull/7",
        "changed_files_count": 4,
        "merge_commit_sha": "d258c686f58713a5eb5167f4e1ad84e2e2ad8df2"
      }
    ],
    "linked_commits": [
      {
        "sha": "de79acaa918c45df358faec1dfbb04b43ef4ab80",
        "message": "fix header inclusion issues on STM32U545 series\n\nResolves https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32u5xx_hal_driver/issues/6\n\nIn trying to get Zephyr RTOS working on the Nucleo U545RE-Q board,\nI discovered header inclusion issues building the HAL for the\nSTM32U545 SoC.\n\nZephyr RTOS makes use of the \"stm32u5xx_hal_driver\" for some\ninteractions with the ST hardware, and builds the HAL by\ncopying the default \"stm32_hal_conf_template.h\" to \"stm32_hal_conf.h\",\nleaving all options enabled.\n\nHowever, some of the modules (specifically HAL_SRAM_MODULE_ENABLED,\nHAL_NAND_MODULE_ENABLED and HAL_NOR_MODULE_ENABLED) do not compile\nfor the STM32U545. Based on recommendations from a engineer in the\nZephyr forums, I modeled changes to four files ((stm32u5xx_hal_sram.h,\nstm32u5xx_hal_nor.h, stm32u5xx_hal_nand.h and stm32u5xx_ll_fmc.h) with\nappropriate \"#ifdef\" checks using the example for the \"stm32g4xx_hal_driver\",\nand this allows the code to build for the U545 series.",
        "committed_at": "2024-02-29T00:13:13Z",
        "github_url": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32u5xx-hal-driver/commit/de79acaa918c45df358faec1dfbb04b43ef4ab80",
        "pr_numbers": [
          7
        ],
